dial_in.body:
I have a rough idea and I want to dial it in before any work happens — like plan mode in Codex/Claude Code. {TASK}

Work with me in this order, and do NOT start executing until I approve the plan:
1. Restate what you think I'm asking for, in your own words.
2. List your assumptions and the unknowns that would change the approach.
3. Ask me up to 3 clarifying questions — the ones whose answers matter most.
4. Propose 2-3 approaches with trade-offs and recommend one.
5. Write a short numbered plan for the recommended approach, with what done looks like for each step.
6. Wait for my approval, then execute one step at a time, checking in after each.

What I know so far: {INPUTS}
Constraints: {CONSTRAINTS}

troubleshoot.body:
Help me troubleshoot and fix this. {TASK}

Known context: {INPUTS}

Work it systematically:
1. Tell me what to confirm first: exact symptom, scope (one user or many), and since when.
2. List the most likely causes for these symptoms, ranked, and say why.
3. For each cause: the exact check or command to run, and what result confirms or rules it out — cheapest checks first.
4. Check what changed recently (updates, policies, passwords, certificates) before assuming hardware or reinstalls.
5. Give the fix for the confirmed cause, then how to verify with the affected user, and what to document.

Change one variable at a time. Constraints: {CONSTRAINTS}
